    "Four"
   ],
   "answer": "Three",
   "explain": "ng counts as one letter, so pang and ngin both fit."
  },
  {
   "type": "choice",
   "q": "A grave mark (`) on the last vowel, as in punò, means…",
   "options": [
    "Penultimate stress with a glottal catch",
    "Stress on the last syllable",
    "A long vowel"
   ],
   "answer": "Penultimate stress with a glottal catch",
   "explain": "Stress the next-to-last syllable and close the throat at the end."
  },
  {
   "type": "choice",
   "q": "A circumflex (^) on the last vowel, as in punô, means…",
   "options": [
    "An end glottal catch with no stress",
    "Stress on the first syllable",
    "A silent letter"
   ],
   "answer": "An end glottal catch with no stress",
   "explain": "The word is said faster and ends with a glottal catch."
  },
