  "Four kinds of syllable: V, CV, VC, CVC. No syllable has more than three letters (ng counts as one).",
  "Four stress types: end stress (´), penultimate stress (´), penultimate with a glottal catch (`), end glottal catch (^).",
  "In the sound guide, CAPITALS are the stressed syllable and Q is the glottal catch.",
  "Stress can change meaning, so learn it with every word.",
  "The glottal catch is lost with a suffix; one-syllable words take the stress before them; a hyphen marks a glottal stop."
